                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Court Chancery Decree of</hi> 23<hi
                        rendition="#italic">d February</hi>, 1833, <hi rendition="#italic">to all
                        the Chief National Authorities, in pursuance of the Imperial Resolution
                        of</hi> 26<hi rendition="#italic">th January</hi>, 1833.</head>
                <p>His Imperial Royal Majesty has been pleased to decide, in addition to the methods
                    of acquiring Austrian citizenship in the General Code of Civil Law, and in
                    accordance with section 32 thereof, and with section 19 of the Emigration Patent
                    of 24th March, 1832, (I. G. S., No. 2,557,) that Austrian citizenship may also
                    be acquired by a foreign woman through her marriage with an Austrian
                    citizen.</p>
            </div>
